{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a0cef26ceec509adb","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Abc4om6RJACTeuCkd4Zxte","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-8OUheG/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-translate-8OUheG-translated-rust/f5816e8b-06f7-42e5-8076-26746ab24d9f/tasks/a0cef26ceec509adb.output","summary":"Done.\n\n## What was done\n\n`src/auto_possess.rs` is a complete literal transliteration of `c_src/src/pcre2_auto_possess.c` (1416 lines C → **1383 lines Rust**), replacing the stub.\n\n**Contents (in C order):**\n- `MAX_LIST`, `APTROWS` (=17), `APTCOLS` (=21) as plain consts derived from `LAST_AUTOTAB_LEFT_OP/LAST_AUTOTAB_RIGHT_OP/FIRST_AUTOTAB_OP`.\n- Static tables reproduced element-for-element: `autoposstab: [[u8;21];17]`, `propposstab: [[u8;PT_TABSIZE];PT_TABSIZE]` (13×13), `catposstab: [[u8;30];7]`, `posspropstab: [[u8;4];3]` (built from `ucp_*` constants).\n- `hspace_case()` / `vspace_case()` helpers expanding the `HSPACE_CASES` / `VSPACE_CASES` macro case-label lists (non-EBCDIC variants: HT/SPACE/NBSP + 0x1680,0x180e,0x2000-0x200a,0x202f,0x205f,0x3000; LF/VT/FF/CR/NEL + 0x2028,0x2029).\n- Private `unsafe fn`s: `check_char_prop`, `get_repeat_base`, `get_chr_property_list`, `compare_opcodes` (recursive).\n- Exported `_pcre2_auto_possessify_8` with the original signature.\n\n**Fidelity notes:**\n- Preserved the `OP_WORDCHAR` `chr < 255` (vs 256) asymmetry, the `OP_NCLASS`→`OP_CLASS` switch fall-through, the `invert_bits` fall-throughs in the bitset dispatch, C `int`-valued boolean comparisons (`(expr) == negated`, `lisprop == (…)`), and the uninitialized-then-conditionally-set `list[4]` pattern.\n- `switch`/`goto` structure modelled with `loop`/`continue`/if-chains keeping the exact order of checks; the outer `for(;;)` in both `compare_opcodes` and `_pcre2_auto_possessify_8` is a `loop`.\n- `#ifdef SUPPORT_JIT/PCRE2_DEBUG/EBCDIC` omitted; `SUPPORT_UNICODE`, `SUPPORT_WIDE_CHARS`, `MAYBE_UTF_MULTI` and the `PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH == 8` `OP_NCLASS` special-casing all included.\n- Cross-module calls: `crate::xclass::_pcre2_xclass_8` / `_pcre2_eclass_8`, `crate::tables::{_pcre2_OP_lengths_8,_pcre2_ucp_gentype_8}`, `crate::ucd_data::_pcre2_ucd_caseless_sets_8`, `script_set_bit` (for `MAPBIT(PRIV(ucd_script_sets)+…)`), `GET_UCD`/`UCD_OTHERCASE`/`UCD_SCRIPTX_PROP`, `getutf8inc` for `GETCHARINCTEST`.\n- `PRIV(find_bracket)` and `PRIV(hspace_list)`/`PRIV(vspace_list)` turned out **not** to be used by this C file, so they aren't referenced.\n\n## Verification\n- `cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"auto_possess.rs\" -B2 -A6` → **no output** (zero errors/warnings attributable to this file).\n- The only remaining crate error is `E0695` in `src/convert.rs:189` (another agent's file, untouched). To prove my module fully type-checks and links, I built an isolated copy of the crate in `$TMPDIR` with `convert.rs` stubbed: it compiled cleanly and `nm -D --defined-only` showed `T _pcre2_auto_possessify_8`. Temp copy deleted.\n- `grep -c \"unimplemented!\\|todo!\" src/auto_possess.rs` → **0**.","usage":{"total_tokens":143738,"tool_uses":24,"duration_ms":592423},"uuid":"173071f6-5958-4f9f-81c1-2f5a3a6e8cc0","session_id":"f5816e8b-06f7-42e5-8076-26746ab24d9f"}
