{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018oKtsYtE8rGyq1pM86N6kR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PCRE2 C -> Rust translation guide (READ THIS FIRST)\n2\t\n3\tWe are transliterating the PCRE2 10.48 C library in `c_src/` into a Rust cdylib in\n4\t`src/`. The build is **8-bit code unit width**, `SUPPORT_UNICODE` defined,\n5\t`SUPPORT_JIT` **not** defined, `EBCDIC` **not** defined, `PCRE2_DEBUG` **not**\n6\tdefined, `LINK_SIZE == 2`, `IMM2_SIZE == 2`, `HAVE_CONFIG_H` defined.\n7\t\n8\t**GOAL: byte-identical behaviour.** This is a *literal transliteration*, not a\n9\trewrite. Do NOT restructure algorithms, do NOT fix bugs, do NOT reorder error\n10\tchecks. Keep the same variable names as the C where possible so the code can be\n11\tdiffed against the C by a human.\n12\t\n13\t## Hard rules\n14\t\n15\t1. Use raw pointers and `unsafe`, mirroring the C 1:1.\n16\t   - `PCRE2_SPTR` -> `*const u8`, `PCRE2_UCHAR *` -> `*mut u8`\n17\t   - `PCRE2_SIZE` -> `usize`, `BOOL` -> `c_int` (with `TRUE`/`FALSE` consts)\n18\t   - `int` -> `c_int`, `unsigned int` -> `c_uint`/`u32`, `uint32_t` -> `u32`, etc.\n19\t2. Every function that the C exports (i.e. is not `static`) must be\n20\t   `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn <FINAL_LINKER_NAME>(...)`.\n21\t   The final linker name has the `_8` suffix applied by the `PCRE2_SUFFIX` macro.\n22\t   Check `nm` names in `SYMBOLS.txt`. Note the irregular ones without an\n23\t   underscore before the 8, e.g. `_pcre2_compile_get_hash_from_name8`,\n24\t   `_pcre2_posix_class_maps8`.\n25\t3. `static` C functions become private `unsafe fn` in the module.\n26\t4. Arithmetic: the crate is built with `overflow-checks = false`, so `+`/`-`/`*`\n27\t   wrap like C. Prefer `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_sub` where the C intent is\n28\t   clearly modular, but plain operators are acceptable. NEVER use checked math\n29\t   that changes behaviour.\n30\t5. Pointer arithmetic:\n31\t   - `p + n` -> `p.add(n)` (or `p.offset(n as isize)` if `n` may be negative)\n32\t   - `p - q` -> `p.offset_from(q)` (gives `isize`); when the C stores this in a\n33\t     `PCRE2_SIZE` use `p.offset_from(q) as usize`.\n34\t   - `*p++` -> `{ let v = *p; p = p.add(1); v }`\n35\t   - `*++p` -> `{ p = p.add(1); *p }`\n36\t   - `*p--` / `*--p` similarly.\n37\t   - Comparing pointers with `<`, `>=` etc. works directly on raw pointers.\n38\t6. `goto` must be translated with Rust control flow. Preferred idioms:\n39\t   - forward `goto LABEL;` where LABEL is at the end of a region:\n40\t     `'label: { ... break 'label; ... }` then the code after the block.\n41\t   - backward goto (loop): `'label: loop { ... continue 'label; ... break; }`\n42\t   - When a C function has a big `for(;;)` with `goto` targets inside a switch,\n43\t     model it exactly with labelled blocks/loops. Keep the structure.\n44\t7. `memcpy`/`memmove`/`memset`/`memchr`/`memcmp`/`malloc`/`free`/`strlen` are\n45\t   declared in `crate::internal` as `extern \"C\"` bindings to libc; call them\n46\t   exactly as the C does (`memcpy(dst as *mut c_void, src as *const c_void, n)`).\n47\t8. File-scope C `static const` tables become `static` items in the Rust module\n48\t   (private). Do not add `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` to them.\n49\t9. Do not add extra bounds checks or `assert!`. `PCRE2_ASSERT`,\n50\t   `PCRE2_DEBUG_UNREACHABLE`, `PCRE2_UNREACHABLE` are all no-ops in this build;\n51\t   translate them to nothing (or a comment).\n52\t10. `PCRE2_FALLTHROUGH` is nothing. C `switch` fallthrough must be replicated\n53\t    explicitly (duplicate the code or restructure with an inner labelled block).\n54\t11. Anything inside `#ifdef SUPPORT_JIT`, `#ifdef PCRE2_DEBUG`,\n55\t    `#ifdef EBCDIC`, `#ifdef SUPPORT_VALGRIND`, `#if PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH != 8`\n56\t    is **omitted**. Anything inside `#ifdef SUPPORT_UNICODE`,\n57\t    `#ifdef SUPPORT_WIDE_CHARS`, `#ifdef MAYBE_UTF_MULTI`,\n58\t    `#if PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH == 8` is **included**.\n59\t\n60\t## What the foundation already provides\n61\t\n62\t`src/internal.rs` (`use crate::internal::*;`) has:\n63\t\n64\t- All types/structs, laid out to match C byte-for-byte (verified with\n65\t  `offset_of!` tests): `pcre2_memctl`, `pcre2_real_general_context`,\n66\t  `pcre2_real_compile_context`, `pcre2_real_match_context`,\n67\t  `pcre2_real_convert_context`, `pcre2_real_code`, `pcre2_real_match_data`,\n68\t  `heapframe` (+ `hf_fields` union and its `hf_*` member structs),\n69\t  `match_block`, `dfa_match_block`, `compile_block`, `class_bits_storage`\n70\t  (union with `.classbits: [u8;32]` / `.classwords: [u32;8]`),\n71\t  `pcre2_callout_block`, `pcre2_callout_enumerate_block`,\n72\t  `pcre2_substitute_callout_block`, `ucd_record`, `ucp_type_table`,\n73\t  `named_group`, `open_capitem`, `compile_data`, `class_ranges`,\n74\t  `recurse_arguments`, `eclass_op_info`, `recurse_check`,\n75\t  `parsed_recurse_check`, `recurse_cache`, `branch_chain`,\n76\t  `dfa_recursion_info`, `pcre2_serialized_data`, `pcre2_real_jit_stack`.\n77\t- Function-pointer typedefs: `MallocFn`, `FreeFn`, `CalloutFn`,\n78\t  `SubstCalloutFn`, `SubstCaseCalloutFn`, `StackGuardFn` (all `Option<unsafe\n79\t  extern \"C\" fn ...>` so that `NULL` is `None`).\n80\t- All `OP_*` opcode constants (as `u32`), `ESC_*` (as `c_int`), `PT_*`, `XCL_*`,\n81\t  `ECL_*`, `CHAR_*` (as `u32`), `cbit_*`, `ctype_*`, `*_offset`,\n82\t  `PCRE2_MODE8`.., `NLTYPE_*`, `MAGIC_NUMBER`, `TABLES_LENGTH`,\n83\t  `START_FRAMES_SIZE`, `DFA_START_RWS_SIZE`, `IMM2_SIZE`, `LINK_SIZE`,\n84\t  `MAX_PATTERN_SIZE`, `MAX_MARK`, `MAX_UTF_SINGLE_CU`, `MAX_UTF_CODE_POINT`,\n85\t  `MAX_NON_UTF_CHAR`, `NOTACHAR`, `LOOKBEHIND_MAX`, `REQ_CU_MAX`,\n86\t  `ECLASS_NEST_LIMIT`, `HEAPFRAME_ALIGNMENT`, `RREF_ANY`, `REFI_FLAG_*`,\n87\t  `PCRE2_OPTIM_*`, config values (`HEAP_LIMIT`, `MATCH_LIMIT`,\n88\t  `MATCH_LIMIT_DEPTH`, `MAX_NAME_COUNT`, `MAX_NAME_SIZE`, `MAX_VARLOOKBEHIND`,\n89\t  `NEWLINE_DEFAULT`, `PARENS_NEST_LIMIT`, `BSR_DEFAULT`).\n90\t- Inline helpers replacing C macros:\n91\t  - `GET(a,n) -> u32`, `PUT(a,n,d)`, `GET2(a,n) -> u32`, `PUT2(a,n,d)`\n92\t    (all `unsafe`, take `*const u8`/`*mut u8`)\n93\t  - `CU2BYTES(x)`, `BYTES2CU(x)` (identity in 8-bit)\n94\t  - `HASUTF8EXTRALEN(c)`, `HAS_EXTRALEN(c)`, `NOT_FIRSTCU(c)`,\n95\t    `GET_EXTRALEN(c)`, `MAX_255(c)`, `CHMAX_255(c)`, `TABLE_GET(c,table,def)`\n96\t  - `getutf8(c, eptr) -> u32` — the `GETUTF8` macro: `eptr` points at the\n97\t    *leading* byte, `c` is that leading byte's value.\n98\t  - `utf8_extra(c) -> usize` — how many extra bytes `getutf8` consumed\n99\t    (use for `GETUTF8LEN`: `len += utf8_extra(c)`).\n100\t  - `getutf8inc(c, eptr) -> (u32, *const u8)` — the `GETUTF8INC` macro:\n101\t    `c` is the already-consumed leading byte, `eptr` points just past it;\n102\t    returns the char and the advanced pointer.\n103\t  - `PUTCHAR(utf: bool, c, p) -> usize`\n104\t  - UCD: `GET_UCD(ch) -> &'static ucd_record`, `UCD_CHARTYPE`, `UCD_SCRIPT`,\n105\t    `UCD_CATEGORY`, `UCD_GRAPHBREAK`, `UCD_CASESET`, `UCD_OTHERCASE`,\n106\t    `UCD_SCRIPTX`, `UCD_BPROPS`, `UCD_BIDICLASS`, `UCD_SCRIPTX_PROP`,\n107\t    `UCD_BIDICLASS_PROP`, `UCD_BPROPS_PROP`, `UCD_ANY_I`, `UCD_DOTTED_I`,\n108\t    `UCD_FOLD_I_TURKISH`, `UCD_BLOCK_SIZE`, `UCD_SCRIPTX_MASK`,\n109\t    `UCD_BIDICLASS_SHIFT`, `UCD_BPROPS_MASK`\n110\t  - `MAPBIT(map,n)`, `script_set_bit(offset,n) -> bool`,\n111\t    `boolprop_set_bit(offset,n) -> bool`, `SETBIT(a,b)`,\n112\t    `CLIST_ALIGN_TO(base,align)`\n113\t- `SyncPtr(*const c_char)` wrapper for exported pointer statics.\n114\t\n115\tCommon convenience for GETCHAR-family macros (write these inline in your module,\n116\tthey are only a couple of lines):\n117\t\n118\t```rust\n119\t// GETCHAR(c, eptr):        let mut c = *eptr as u32; if c >= 0xc0 { c = getutf8(c, eptr); }\n120\t// GETCHARTEST(c, eptr):    let mut c = *eptr as u32; if utf && c >= 0xc0 { c = getutf8(c, eptr); }\n121\t// GETCHARINC(c, eptr):     let mut c = *eptr as u32; eptr = eptr.add(1);\n122\t//                          if c >= 0xc0 { let r = getutf8inc(c, eptr); c = r.0; eptr = r.1; }\n123\t// GETCHARINCTEST(c, eptr): same but `if utf && c >= 0xc0`\n124\t// GETCHARLEN(c, eptr, len): let mut c = *eptr as u32;\n125\t//                          if c >= 0xc0 { len += utf8_extra(c); c = getutf8(c, eptr); }\n126\t// GETCHARLENTEST: same but `if utf && c >= 0xc0`\n127\t// BACKCHAR(eptr):          while (*eptr & 0xc0) == 0x80 { eptr = eptr.sub(1); }\n128\t// FORWARDCHAR(eptr):       while (*eptr & 0xc0) == 0x80 { eptr = eptr.add(1); }\n129\t// FORWARDCHARTEST(eptr,end): while eptr < end && (*eptr & 0xc0) == 0x80 { eptr = eptr.add(1); }\n130\t// ACROSSCHAR(cond, eptr, act): while (cond) && (*eptr & 0xc0) == 0x80 { act }\n131\t```\n132\t\n133\t## Data tables (already generated, do not re-derive)\n134\t\n135\t`crate::tables`:\n136\t`_pcre2_OP_lengths_8: [u8;173]`, `_pcre2_default_tables_8: [u8;1088]`,\n137\t`_pcre2_hspace_list_8: [u32;_]`, `_pcre2_vspace_list_8: [u32;_]`,\n138\t`_pcre2_callout_start_delims_8: [u32;_]`, `_pcre2_callout_end_delims_8: [u32;_]`,\n139\t`_pcre2_ucp_gentype_8: [u32;32]`, `_pcre2_ucp_gbtable_8: [u32;16]`,\n140\t`_pcre2_utf8_table1: [c_int;6]`, `_pcre2_utf8_table1_size: c_uint`,\n141\t`_pcre2_utf8_table2: [c_int;6]`, `_pcre2_utf8_table3: [c_int;6]`,\n142\t`_pcre2_utf8_table4: [u8;64]`, `_pcre2_posix_class_maps8: [c_int;42]`\n143\t\n144\t`crate::ucd_data`:\n145\t`_pcre2_ucd_caseless_sets_8: [u32;_]`, `_pcre2_ucd_turkish_dotted_i_caseset_8: u32`,\n146\t`_pcre2_ucd_nocase_ranges_8: [u32;_]`, `_pcre2_ucd_nocase_ranges_size_8: u32`,\n147\t`_pcre2_ucd_digit_sets_8: [u32;_]`, `_pcre2_ucd_script_sets_8: [u32;_]`,\n148\t`_pcre2_ucd_boolprop_sets_8: [u32;_]`, `_pcre2_ucd_records_8: [ucd_record;_]`,\n149\t`_pcre2_ucd_stage1_8: [u16;_]`, `_pcre2_ucd_stage2_8: [u16;_]`,\n150\t`_pcre2_utt_names_8: [u8;_]`, `_pcre2_utt_8: [ucp_type_table;518]`,\n151\t`_pcre2_utt_size_8: usize`, `_pcre2_unicode_version_8: SyncPtr`\n152\t\n153\t`crate::ucp`: every `uc