pe_retry: loop` plus a `goto_escape_failed` flag.\n- `goto FROM_PERL_EXTENDED_CLASS` (from `(?[`) → `'sw` is a `loop`; sets `sw_target = 1` and `continue 'sw`, and the dispatcher re-enters via `break 'l_from_perl_extended_class`. This required moving the class-parsing block (C 3951–4712) to the end of the block chain, which is safe because nothing jumps into or out of it forwards.\n\nAdditionally the class loop uses `'class_loop` / `'class_continue` / `'class_literal` for `CLASS_CONTINUE` / `CLASS_LITERAL`, and the function-level labels `FAILED`, `FAILED_BACK`, `FAILED_FORWARD`, `UNCLOSED_PARENTHESIS`, `PARSED_END` are five nested labelled blocks around the whole body.\n\n## Notable details\n\n- `PARSED_LITERAL(c,p)` expanded inline as `*p = c; p = p.add(1); okquantifier = TRUE;` — all 10 macro sites verified to be in contexts where both statements execute (the macro is unbraced in C).\n- `PUTOFFSET` expanded to the two-word 64-bit form (SIZEOFFSET == 2).\n- `IS_NEWLINE(ptr)` expanded with `NLBLOCK == cb`, `PSEND == end_pattern`, calling `crate::newline::_pcre2_is_newline_8`.\n- Omitted, as instructed: all `#ifdef PCRE2_DEBUG` bounds bookkeeping (`parsed_pattern_extra`, `parsed_pattern_check`, `ptr_check`), `PCRE2_ASSERT`, the `NEVER_BACKSLASH_C` / `#ifndef SUPPORT_UNICODE` branches (ERR85, ERR96, 3×ERR45), and `META_BIGVALUE` (32-bit-only).\n- `cb->class_op_used[class_depth_m1]` is accessed via raw-pointer `offset()` rather than array indexing, so a hypothetical negative index behaves like C (OOB read) instead of panicking on a Rust bounds check.\n- Local `nest_save` struct defined in the module (`4×u16 + 2×u32` = 16 bytes, align 4, matching C, which matters for the `end_nests` rounding arithmetic), plus `NSF_*`, `PARSE_TRACKED_*`, `RANGE_*`, `CLASS_OP_*`, `CLASS_MODE_*`, and the string constants `[:<:]]`, `[:>:]]`, `Q\\E`, `VERSION`, `DEFINE`.\n\n## Verification performed beyond compiling\n\nFrequency-diffed the C region against the Rust for every `ERRnn`, every `