e 8256 (`case META_CAPTURE` → `GROUP_PROCESS_NOTE_EMPTY`) which conflicts with the forward goto at 7157 (`HANDLE_NUMERICAL_RECURSION`). Placing all arms in the innermost block breaks that cycle without needing a loop/state variable.\n- `OUTPUT_SINGLE_REPEAT` (C 7883) sits *inside* the `REPEAT` region within the `default:` arm of `switch(op_previous)`, and control jumps into that C block. Modelled with `'AFTER_OP_SWITCH { 'PROP_DONE { 'OUTPUT_SINGLE_REPEAT { … } prop_type=prop_value=-1 } …rest… }`, with `prop_type`/`prop_value`/`oldcode` hoisted to loop scope.\n- C fallthroughs replicated explicitly: `META_PRUNE`→`META_COMMIT`, `META_PRUNE_ARG`→`VERB_ARG`, `META_NOCAPTURE`→`GPNE`, `ESC_B/b`→`ESC_A`. The large `OP_RECURSE`→bracket-group fallthrough (C 7692) was handled by merging both cases into one arm guarded by `if op_previous == OP_RECURSE`, avoiding ~150 lines of duplication while preserving order.\n\n### Fidelity notes\n- Unsigned wraparound preserved with `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_sub` at every `OFLOW_MAX - *lengthptr` comparison and length accumulation.\n- `META_CALLOUT_STRING` pre-compile length uses u32 arithmetic before widening, matching C's integer promotions (`pptr[3] + (1+4*LINK_SIZE)` is `unsigned int` in C).\n- Apparent quirks kept as-is, e.g. `*previous++ = OP_SKIPZERO` advancing `previous` right before `goto END_REPEAT`, and `case META_COND_RNUMBER` rewriting `start_pptr[0] = meta | 1`.\n- Omitted per build config: `SUPPORT_JIT`, `PCRE2_DEBUG`, `EBCDIC`, `PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH != 32` branches; `PCRE2_ASSERT`/`PCRE2_DEBUG_UNREACHABLE` are no-ops.\n\n### Only compile fix needed\n`LOOKBEHIND_MAX` is `c_int` in `internal.rs` but compared against a `u32` in `compile_regex`; added an `as u32` cast (matches C's usual-arithmetic-conversion behaviour).","usage":{"total_tokens":201989,"tool_uses":53,"duration_ms":1142191},"uuid":"31f3c890-3b3e-40c0-b89d-4e315763c652","session_id":"f5816e8b-06f7-42e5-8076-26746ab24d9f"}
