{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_z6psn7h55dvqrsoea7ft36ouce5an3xsqsr2gwxzwow5m4prdvqa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The translation is complete and verified. \n\n## What was done\n\nPCRE2 10.48-DEV (~74k lines of C, 8-bit code-unit build, `SUPPORT_UNICODE`, no JIT, `LINK_SIZE=2`) translated to a Rust cdylib: **51,647 lines across 51 Rust modules**.\n\n### Completion gate: symbol diff is empty\n```\nC  exports: 143      Rust exports: 143\ndiff <C symbols> <Rust symbols>  ->  *** EMPTY ***\nSymbol types also match exactly: 112 T, 27 R, 4 D in both\n```\nAll the macro-generated names are reproduced, including the irregular ones without an underscore before the width suffix (`_pcre2_posix_class_maps8`, `_pcre2_compile_get_hash_from_name8`, `_pcre2_compile_parse_recurse_args8`, …).\n\n### Structure\n- `internal.rs` — every struct laid out to match C **byte-for-byte** (verified by `offset_of!`/`size_of` unit tests against `offsetof` output from a C probe: `pcre2_real_code` 152 B, `heapframe` fields@32/eptr@64/ovector@120, `match_block` 272 B, `compile_block` 360 B, …). This matters because `pcre2_serialize_encode` writes the struct out and `PCRE2_INFO_SIZE`/`FRAMESIZE` expose its size.\n- Data tables (`tables.rs`, `ucd_data.rs`, `compile_tables.rs`) were **generated mechanically** by C dumper programs, not transcribed.\n- `pcre2_match.c`'s 6,300-line `match()` (72 `RMATCH`/395 `RRETURN` gotos) became a flat `lbl`-driven dispatch loop in `matcher_core.rs`, with the opcode switch split across 11 `include!`-spliced chunk files.\n- `pcre2_compile.c` split into `compile_tables/compile_util/compile_parse/compile_branch/compile.rs`.\n\n### Verification against the C `.so`\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| All 27 exported data tables + 3 default contexts, byte-compared | **identical** |\n| Full API harness (130 patterns × 29 option sets × 42 subjects × 9 match options, both matchers, callouts, substring APIs, substitute, serialize incl. **full compiled-bytecode hex**) | **1,958,374 lines identical** |\n| Compile-path fuzz (random patterns, comparing errcode/erroroffset/serialized bytecode) | **4.4 M patterns, 0 mismatches** |\n| Match fuzz (`pcre2_match` + `pcre2_dfa_match` + `pcre2_substitute`, incl. random raw-byte subjects) | **~3.3 M checks, 0 mismatches** |\n| Pathological patterns (260-deep nesting, 70k captures, 20k alternations, huge/wide classes, name-table & size limits) | **identical** |\n| Internal helpers, exhaustive (`ord2utf` over 0..0x11FFFF, `valid_utf` over all 1–3 byte strings, newline/extuni/script_run/string utils) | **identical** |\n| Custom-allocator accounting (malloc/free call counts and byte totals) | **identical** |\n\nBugs/quirks in the C were deliberately reproduced (e.g. `PCRE2_CONFIG_COMPILED_WIDTHS` returning 0 because `SUPPORT_PCRE2_8` isn't in this `config.h`; `*errorptr = ERR0` on success; over-allocation by `* PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH` instead of `CU2BYTES` in `substring_get_bynumber`/`pattern_convert`; the dead `Lextra_size` macro).\n\n`c_src/` was not modified. `TRANSLATION_GUIDE.md`, `MATCHER_CORE.md` and `SYMBOLS.txt` are left in place as documentation of the translation contract and the definition of done."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1319,"cache_read_input_tokens":707529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1319,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5816e8b-06f7-42e5-8076-26746ab24d9f","uuid":"0492b004-08d0-47dc-8f6e-b20bcaac74ad","timestamp":"2026-08-22T16:33:23.524Z"}
